{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there","id":904393,"title":"How many Solar tombs are there?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T13:31:14-07:00","id":904393,"title":"How many Solar tombs are there?","content":"I am <b>not</b> looking for an exact number or even an official estimate. This topic is more about... well, maybe I should explain it differently.<br /> <br /> We know there exist Solar tombs, wherein previous incarnations are buried along with their panoplies of weapons and armor and stuff. We know they're usually trapped and guarded to hell. It feels like it's been stated both ways that 1) the Dragon-Blooded created them to house the slain Solars after the Usurpation to sedate their hungry ghosts, and 2) the Solars made them to supplement their vanity.<br /> <br /> So when Solar Joe created a Tomb for himself and his future incarnations and then died, Solar Jim (his next incarnation) goes into the Tomb and gets his stuff. What happens when Solar Jim dies? Does he get put in Joe's Tomb? Or does Joe get his OWN Tomb? Where does Solar James go (Joe's 3rd incarnation) to get his cool stuff? Where does James get buried?<br /> <br /> I guess my question is, are there roughly 300 or so Tombs out there, likely built after the Usurpation, or are there probably hundreds or even thousands from many of the Solars that have ever been? I doubt there's one every few hundred square miles of Creation or anything, but I'm curious how people view this issue. Again, I'm not expecting an canon answer, just a discussion of possibility/likelihood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:40:30-07:00","id":904403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there#post904393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am <b>not</b> looking for an exact number or even an official estimate. This topic is more about... well, maybe I should explain it differently.<br /> <br /> We know there exist Solar tombs, wherein previous incarnations are buried along with their panoplies of weapons and armor and stuff. We know they're usually trapped and guarded to hell. It feels like it's been stated both ways that 1) the Dragon-Blooded created them to house the slain Solars after the Usurpation to sedate their hungry ghosts, and 2) the Solars made them to supplement their vanity.<br /> <br /> So when Solar Joe created a Tomb for himself and his future incarnations and then died, Solar Jim (his next incarnation) goes into the Tomb and gets his stuff. What happens when Solar Jim dies? Does he get put in Joe's Tomb? Or does Joe get his OWN Tomb? Where does Solar James go (Joe's 3rd incarnation) to get his cool stuff? Where does James get buried?<br /> <br /> I guess my question is, are there roughly 300 or so Tombs out there, likely built after the Usurpation, or are there probably hundreds or even thousands from many of the Solars that have ever been? I doubt there's one every few hundred square miles of Creation or anything, but I'm curious how people view this issue. Again, I'm not expecting an canon answer, just a discussion of possibility/likelihood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it varies from Exaltation to Exaltation. I really doubt that they think of themselves as the same person to such an extent. And vanity would often demand you own, new tomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:48:17-07:00","id":904413,"title":"","content":"I remember musing in the backstory to my Dawn that the first incarnation to hold that Exaltation mantle foresaw this problem, and didn't build herself a crypt. She built a <i>mausoleum</i>. The rules were simple. Her successors could, if they get through the front door (which still requires evading a few simple traps and fighting a guardian automaton. You should see the path that trespassers are dumped into) could take any weapon or armor they wanted from the mausoleum. Swords, spears, bows, smashfists, plate, silken armor, it was an entire armory.<br /> <br /> They were of course limited to how many they could take by how well they got through the front door (ST fiat, to keep your players from going Battle Hydra, usually one weapon and one piece of armor) but they were still able to pick something.<br /> <br /> Each artifact within the mausoleum was also enchanted so that when the current holder died, all of their gear from the mausoleum was pulled back to its resting spot within, waiting for the next Exaltation holder.<br /> <br /> This proved very useful, as that particular Dawn's next incarnation quickly became the Circle's Kenny, never lasting more than a decade or so before dying to something brutal. It got to a point where this exchange happened.<br /> <br /> Zenith: Okay, Dawn-<br /> <br /> Dawn: My name is White Tiger.<br /> <br /> Zenith: Yeah, and the one before that was Weeping Lotus, and the one before that was, um...<br /> <br /> Twilight: That was Bull, wasn't it? Bull, Auroch, something bovine.<br /> <br /> Zenith: Right, Something Bull. Point is, your predecessors didn't last long. Make it five years and I <i>might</i> learn your name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:48:54-07:00","id":904415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904403#post904403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say it varies from Exaltation to Exaltation. I really doubt that they think of themselves as the same person to such an extent. And vanity would often demand you own, new tomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you'd say that it wasn't just one generation of tombs made by the Dragon-Blooded, that there are also many made by individual Solars? That's <i>probably</i> the way I'd do it too. But it's an interesting thought process to me. I also like to imagine there were big differences between the Dragon-Blooded designed tombs and the Solar designed tombs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:55:56-07:00","id":904420,"title":"","content":"More than you'd think, but less than you hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T13:58:02-07:00","id":904422,"title":"","content":"Setting answer &quot;One always exists where the story demands one, and never anywhere else.&quot;<br /> <br /> More helpful answer:<br /> <br /> You are correct there are two primary sources of Solar tombs. However, in Ex3, the length, nature, and culture of the First Age are undefined. I think it's safe to say that most of the Solars slain in the Usurpation got a tomb of one kind or another. The Dragon-Bloods built them for a good reason, and they had the time to be thorough. So, we have nearly 300 tombs, there.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I really think you have to consider how common you want them in your Creation and work from there. There are simply too many variables to decide otherwise. If the First Age was ten thousand years long, that's many Solar incarnations, each with a chance at their own tomb. If it was only a thousand years long, then that's far fewer tombs. Additionally, some tombs may be completely lost (destroyed by a cataclysm, lost to the Wyld, etc). And, of course, culturally it's possible not every Solar warranted a great tomb (not every Pharaoh was powerful enough to get a pyramid).<br /> <br /> So, after you control for how many Solars had tombs, and how many of those were lost, you're basically back to playing out a Fermi problem with First Age variables, tossing out a number that feels right, or just not numbering them, and putting them where necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  typo 05-31-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:02:45-07:00","id":904425,"title":"","content":"In 1e, they have many stories about it...saying that the DBs did make a lot of the Solar Tombs and buried their treasures with them, to avoid angry solar ghosts, last thing that they wanted to deal with.<br /> <br /> Some theories/speculations:<br /> <br /> There are also so many possibilities...after a Solar dies, maybe his Lunar mate comes and get the treasures and put them back into the Solar tomb for the next reincarnation to find.<br /> <br /> Also something to think about Solars during the first age, were at peace and lived like emperors...god-kings. It wasn't uncommon for a Solar to have not only multiple Manses, tombs (whoever died during the Primordial wars) , and many solars making sure that everybody got their devices. The First age lasted an indeterminate amount of time but it was apparently enough time in 2e to determine that Solars could die of Old Age, granted after living like thousands of years but still, I wouldn't be surprised that crafter solars, would take their times to make the perfect work or even make artifacts for other Solars just to kill sometime...after all gotta keep busy while nobody can challenge you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:05:35-07:00","id":904429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904415#post904415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you'd say that it wasn't just one generation of tombs made by the Dragon-Blooded, that there are also many made by individual Solars? That's <i>probably</i> the way I'd do it too. But it's an interesting thought process to me. I also like to imagine there were big differences between the Dragon-Blooded designed tombs and the Solar designed tombs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was running a game before personal issues canceled it. Island in the Dreaming Sea, guarded by a massive animated stone serpent. An ancient Solar designed it as a tomb and a deathtrap for the graverobbers he was convinced would come. This was a pre-Usurpation thing, just a mad old Solar worried about his enemies siezing his research for their own purposes. It's the kind of thing I imagine is around here and there. Some more deadly than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:12:04-07:00","id":904435,"title":"","content":"Man, can you imagine remembering where your predecessor's tomb is, and when you get there it's the <i>wrong one</i>? Your immediate preincarnation already robbed it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:44:21-07:00","id":904467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904435#post904435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, can you imagine remembering where your predecessor's tomb is, and when you get there it's the <i>wrong one</i>? Your immediate preincarnation already robbed it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you get there and find out that there's nothing there, with a note that says &quot;Dear future me: Suck it. Ain't giving nobody a handout! Signed, The Guy Who Just Played You&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T16:05:22-07:00","id":904525,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer to find old Solar manse to Solar's Tomb as backstory for items ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:35:05-07:00","id":904582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904525#post904525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I prefer to find old Solar manse to Solar's Tomb as backstory for items ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're typically the same thing in my previous games. Solar has a kickass manse, gets buried in it with their stuff. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:54:11-07:00","id":904630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904582#post904582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they're typically the same thing in my previous games. Solar has a kickass manse, gets buried in it with their stuff. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think that this does not work in 3ed, manses seem to be alot more rare (sice weak manses are no longer a thing) and if they are even remotely as useful as previous edition then it would only be done in extremely important cases. A less charitable example from a 2ed game was that they buried a Solar in her manse because she had become a recluse (read:Otaku) and her DBs couldnt think of anywhere else to bury her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:57:16-07:00","id":904633,"title":"","content":"I always saw it as the Usurption era tombs were always grandoise and trap to high hell in order to appease the hungry ghost and secure the artifacts of said Solar safely away. Any tombs predating the Usurption would be as varied as the Solars they contained. With as many as needed for plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:23:50-07:00","id":904647,"title":"","content":"Here's a second set of rails for this topic. Have you ever had a tomb for a different exalt type in your game? Any Sidereal tombs? Lunar tombs? Dragon-Blooded tombs even? I'm not surprised by the lack of Abyssal tombs, but if Solars used to make their own tombs, why wouldn't there be others as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:35:48-07:00","id":904654,"title":"","content":"In Rathess, in the previous editions, there was a major necropolis of Solar tombs. Thses go all the way back to the Primordal War. I assume that every celestial exalted who died before the usurpation was buried in a major tomb, and that their later incarnations would have the option to reclaim their gear. After the Usurpation, many Solars were buried in lavish tombs to try to keep their ghosts down, and any equipment that survived the fight was buried with them. As a storyteller, I have included things like half a warstrider in a Solar tomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11828-ikari-gendo","name":"Ikari Gendo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:02:17-07:00","id":904667,"title":"","content":"DBs tombs definitely but well, usually there isn't a lot of good stuffs to get from there, as the dynasts usually transfer valuable artifacts to their next of kin at death or even before they pass away. A lot of DBs tombs are relatively recent compared to the history of the world. Some ancient and respected DBs sometime get their hands on Manses of other types of exalts.<br /> <br /> Lunars , who are relevant are still alive...so you are most likely walking into a lion's den and sometime quite literally. There are of course tombs for Lunars...just that the likelihood of finding a lunar tombs that isn't within a Lunar dominion are very slim and relatively easy to access to. Plus due to their abilities to change into beasts and the likes, some Lunars like the ones who can change into underwater creatures make it quite a challenge to even reach their tomb.<br /> <br /> Sidereals have their internships and transferring property going on with their bureaucracy red tape. At least for every future sidereals who play the politics of Yu Shan correctly. Most Sidereals manses are in Yu Shan. There are a few in creation but at least in my version they are the rarest kind of manses (in creation).<br /> <br /> Abyssals are showered with gifts by their angry first age solar ghost of choice and only been active for 5 years in 3e at least.<br /> Infernals just get loot for being green sun princes and ruling Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T21:58:49-07:00","id":904718,"title":"","content":"In my creation while mortals of the realm see humble but sufficient funerary services the dragon blooded themselves receive much grander funerals often with several days of mourning services and celebrations of life and deeds before a procession equal parts parade and mourning escorts the body to the families crypt-palace. These palaces are often large grand homes in the style of the family's ancestral manse. During the days of mourning a personal room is constructed for the deceased Nobel where he is played to rest among the treasures and luxuries he chose not to pass on in will. The crypts are tended by mortal family members trained in the arts of exorcism and care for the dead. Heroes whose bodies were lost are laid to rest in effigy at the least still receiving similar honor. Dragon blooded who died without honor or after being banished are often still laid to rest in modest &quot;by dynasty standards&quot; crypts close to their homes. These family palaces do in fact cast shadows into the underworld where the ghosts of dragon blooded past play their games of Nobel dead. Their constant drives to one up each other keep them divided and weak but should the Nobel houses of dead dragons ever unite they would make quite the notable force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:50:09-07:00","id":904735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904647#post904647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a second set of rails for this topic. Have you ever had a tomb for a different exalt type in your game? Any Sidereal tombs? Lunar tombs? Dragon-Blooded tombs even? I'm not surprised by the lack of Abyssal tombs, but if Solars used to make their own tombs, why wouldn't there be others as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point. My current game I'm running the PCs are headed to a Valley of the Kings type place with something like Ten Anathema tombs situated there. At least one of which is designed pretty much entirely to hold the Solar's ghost inside it (one tomb robber apparently managed to escape and inscribed a warning on the door.) I should include a few Lunar tombs in there. <br /> <br /> Sidereals I tend to presume are interred in Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:23:47-07:00","id":904908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904647#post904647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a second set of rails for this topic. Have you ever had a tomb for a different exalt type in your game? Any Sidereal tombs? Lunar tombs? Dragon-Blooded tombs even? I'm not surprised by the lack of Abyssal tombs, but if Solars used to make their own tombs, why wouldn't there be others as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good point.<br /> <br /> I have included Dragon-Blooded tombs for FA Chosen who were favored servants of Solars, often built around the Solar's tomb. I've also done a twin crypt thing for a Solar/Lunar couple.<br /> <br /> If I had to headcanon some overall trends with a gun to my head, I would go with:<br /> <br /> Dragon-Bloods have the most tombs of any Chosen, with a good chunk from the First Age, and a ton of them from the Shogunate. However, those tombs are more likely to contain &quot;mundane,&quot; wealth and symbolic representations of their possessions, as DBs tend to inherit stuff, rather than bury it. There also plenty of family mausoleums, since DBs value family. In the Realm, I'm thinking the Immaculate Philosophy discourages over-attachment to the dead, reminding people they have finally ascended to unity with the Dragons. Monuments are more common, with tombs only for exceptional (or at least exceptionally powerful and wealthy) individuals.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are fundamentally agents of Heaven. I think the closest offiicial thing they have is a Wall of Honor kinda thing, like the CIA has at their HQ. Unofficially, I'd say friends of the Sid (almost always fellow Sids) will often take time to bury or burn the body somewhere in Creation the deceased loved dearly, or they all pitch in and pay for a tomb in Sijan. In any case, Starmetal is rare, and departmental resources are always tight, so phat lewtz are going to be held by the Bureau, likely for the next incarnation.<br /> <br /> Lunars are going to be the most split. First Age Lunar tombs are probably only slightly less rare than Solars (there are now far more Lunars than Solars, but they were still less likely to get tombs). However, those tombs are on the whole less ostentatious, with a few stand-out exceptions. They may or may not contain magical grave goods, as I headcanon most Lunars in the 2nd Age are pragmatic to a fault, and thus likely to rob tombs at every opportunity. Shogunate and Realm-Era Lunars who fall are likely to be interred in a place of natural beauty, such as under an artistically carved boulder on a mountain-top, or their ashes are scattered at such a place, and the modern tombs are crap for grave goods (what Lunar can afford leaving behind Artifacts?). Due to the ever-shifting lines of the war with the Realm, a tomb built today could be a bathhouse for Dynasts in a century or two, so I don't see Lunars putting much time and effort into &quot;traditional&quot; mausoleums. Exceptions might exist on the Caul or similar places.<br /> <br /> On the whole, only the First Age really afforded the kind of raw weath and privilege required to erect and provision structures we think of when we say &quot;tomb,&quot; because we are likely imagining those structures in Nexus that harbor great wealth and items of magical power. If you broaden the definition, they may become more common, but culture and simple pragmatism is against large, formal construction projects for this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:42:42-07:00","id":904921,"title":"","content":"Arcane Fate may make locating a Sidereal Tomb difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:15:31-07:00","id":904942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904921#post904921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arcane Fate may make locating a Sidereal Tomb difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would Arcane Fate persist after a Sidereal dies? I doubt what is done would be undone, but if mortals witness a Sidereal die (thus not giving Arcane Fate much chance to work) would they remember it clearly afterwards? Or would it still get muddled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:43:28-07:00","id":904958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/904393-how-many-solar-tombs-are-there?p=904942#post904942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would Arcane Fate persist after a Sidereal dies? I doubt what is done would be undone, but if mortals witness a Sidereal die (thus not giving Arcane Fate much chance to work) would they remember it clearly afterwards? Or would it still get muddled?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I head canon that Arcane Fate will eventually erase all evidence of the dead Sidereal's existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:12:25-07:00","id":904998,"title":"","content":"I would imagine sidereals being as secretive as they are wouldn't want the liability of a dead sidereal just lying around; imagine what a deathlord could do with such a find if they could somehow determine that the body belonged to a sidereal.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking dead sidereals are cremated as a routine policy probably at night when their maiden is visible in the sky. Not sure what to do with the ashes, but I wouldn't want them concentrated in one place. I say the ashes are spread out someplace special. Perhaps at a sidereal demesne.<br /> <br /> Back in the first age when all the enemies of creation were cowed and beaten and before arcane fate, sidereals probably had elaborate tombs like the other celestial exalted. After arcane fate went into effect no one could remember who the sidereal tombs were for. But such tombs every bit as elaborate as lunar tombs would probably lead many an individual to wonder for whom such tombs were constructed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:43:38-07:00","id":905110,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that most of the big dungeon tombs are Solar. Dragon-blooded pass their goods back to their family, and probably are interred in the family mausoleum. Great heroes probably get more than an average family member in terms of space, but that's probably about it. I suspect most Lunars don't like the idea of a permanent structure. I've always viewed them as more attuned to the cycle of reincarnation, and don't need the sort of immortality in death that a god-king needs. I also don't think Sidereals need much in terms of tombs. I do envision a 'heroe's graveyard' in Heaven where dead Sids are buried in reward for their service, with a memorial wall. Sids are probably pretty good about having their goods handed down to whom they want to have them, rather than be buried with them. Abyssals build them now and live in them. Infernals will very much build great tombs if they get the chance. <br /> <br /> As always, exceptions exist. There will be first age Lunar tombs built by Solars, for example, but I picture most Lunars considering them gauche. There will always be the DB general who conquered enough territory that he can rule it like a god-king of old and build a great tomb... but it probably becomes a mausoleum for his family after a few generations. Or it becomes the centrepiece of a Valley of Kings type thing, which is really the same thing, but on a bigger scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T23:15:16-07:00","id":906239,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of a multi-tiered tomb, representing multiple incarnations of a single Solar Essence, before the Usurpation. At the Usurpation, the entire tomb was filled with the Wonders, Trophies, etc. of the Solar, and then sealed.<br /> <br /> You may find sections that have collapsed, sections that have been stripped by previous incarnations, the Solar's Lunar mate, Sidereals trying to preserve certain Wonders, or keep them from falling into the wrong hands, grave robbers, etc., etc. There could be just about anything in there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11910-wick-black","name":"Wick Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}